# glyph-fit-default: the font set of the glyph-fit page (tools/vt/sections/56-glyph-fit.sh)
# with every fit= left at its default. DejaVu Sans Mono draws the text, and
# Monoid Nerd Font Mono is merged behind it by cover= for the private-use
# ranges where Nerd Fonts and Powerline put their symbols. Its symbols are
# drawn at the size at which Monoid's own ascent and descent span the cell.
# 30 per cent of line spacing makes each row taller, so the page shows how
# each kind of glyph uses the added rows. The files are from Arch Linux's
# ttf-dejavu and ttf-monoid-nerd packages.
#
# Licences: Bitstream Vera for DejaVu Sans Mono; MIT for Monoid and the
# Nerd Fonts patcher, each icon set under its own.
#
# checks: separators the whole cell high; box lines that join; icons and marks in the text band

name=glyph-fit-default
license=Bitstream-Vera AND MIT

source=outline:/usr/share/fonts/TTF/DejaVuSansMono.ttf
source=outline:/usr/share/fonts/TTF/MonoidNerdFontMono-Regular.ttf
cover=U+E000-U+F8FF
cover=U+F0001-U+F1AF0
cover=U+2500-U+257F
source=builtin:unifont
line-spacing=30
